Hint : don't forget where you are at :)

Explanation :
Classical timezone issue.
"2015-04-14 IDT" -> the IDT means Israeli Daylight Time
When you are using POSIXct it also as a notion of hours , and when you give it a date the default for hours is : 0 (meaning midnight)
"as.Date" function also has a timezone parameter which by default is set to UTC (which is 3 hours before IDT as of today).
therefore, the UTC date is actually a day before :)

Fix :
keep it in IDT (if that's what you actually want) :
as.Date(x,tz="Asia/Jerusalem")
OR
when you set the POSIXct date in the first place, put it as UTC :
x<-as.POSIXct("2015-04-14",tz="UTC")
(that way as.Date will work as expected)

Regards,
Daniel Marcous,
Google, Waze, BI, Data Wizard.

